      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1">No page image before p. 10 is available; the chapter in progress is taken from the running head (Kap. I), and no Coptic chapter numeral is visible on this page.</p>
        <p n="1">The framed manuscript page number [ⲓ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="2">The edition prints an opening bracket before ⲧϥ and no closing bracket; the four lost letters are taken to end the restoration before ϣⲃⲱⲛ.</p>
        <p n="3">The ⲥ of ϩⲉⲥⲧϥ is added above the line by a later hand (editor's apparatus).</p>
        <p n="5">The editors suggest ⲡⲕⲉⲡⲁ[ⲧϣⲏⲛ] (apparatus, marked as possible).</p>
        <p n="10">ⲝ (here and in ll. 16, 25) is printed with its detached wavy top bar; this is read as part of the letter, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="15">The edition prints an opening bracket before ⲉ ⲛ̄ⲣⲙ̄ϩⲉ and no closing bracket; the restoration and the eight lost letters are taken to run to the end of the line.</p>
        <p n="19">The editors confirm ⲁⲥϩϥ as the manuscript reading (apparatus: "so").</p>
        <p n="24">The stroke over the restored ⲣ is printed as a peaked (caret-like) stroke, as over ⲣ in l. 25. The space before ⲛ̄ⲧⲉϥⲉⲕⲕⲗⲏⲥⲓⲁ is about twice a normal word space; the editors do not mark it.</p>
        <p n="27">The edition prints a closing bracket after ⲥ with no opening bracket; the eight dots before it are therefore encoded as illegible.</p>
        <p n="30">The bracket opened before ⲟⲥ is closed only in l. 31, after four dots; it is closed here at the line end and reopened in l. 31.</p>
        <p n="31">The bracket before the last five dots is not closed in the edition (l. 32 begins with illegible dots); it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="32">The bracket before the last four dots is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="33">The bracket before the last four dots is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end.</p>
      </div>
